- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests`

**How to implement.** The Items panel, a surface in a file of its own (001 §O 'Items panel: the list, "Add item from library model…", a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance), the dial mapping, revisions'; 001 §O 'Automation': ids such as `KitItemList`; the S7.2 brief: ids `KitItemList`, `AddItemButton`, `ItemParameterGrid` and so on; .spec-md §4 'UI': new surfaces live in their own files; §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the kit-bar group (steps 188, 202, 226), `// --- The Items panel (ItemsPanelView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `itemsPanel` (`"ItemsPanel"`), `kitItemList` (`"KitItemList"`), `addItemButton` (`"AddItemButton"`), `addItemOfferList` (`"AddItemOfferList"`), `newItemLabelField` (`"NewItemLabelField"`), `addItemConfirmButton` (`"AddItemConfirmButton"`), `addItemCancelButton` (`"AddItemCancelButton"`), `itemLabelField` (`"ItemLabelField"`), `itemModelText` (`"ItemModelText"`), `itemDialText` (`"ItemDialText"`), `itemNotesField` (`"ItemNotesField"`), `itemPhotoText` (`"ItemPhotoText"`), `itemChoosePhotoButton` (`"ItemChoosePhotoButton"`), `itemRemovePhotoButton` (`"ItemRemovePhotoButton"`), `itemParameterGrid` (`"ItemParameterGrid"`), `parameterEditPanel` (`"ParameterEditPanel"`), `parameterEditKnownChoice` (`"ParameterEditKnownChoice"`), `parameterEditUnknownChoice` (`"ParameterEditUnknownChoice"`), `parameterEditValueField` (`"ParameterEditValueField"`), `parameterEditLowerField` (`"ParameterEditLowerField"`), `parameterEditUpperField` (`"ParameterEditUpperField"`), `parameterEditPriorSigmaField` (`"ParameterEditPriorSigmaField"`), `parameterEditSetButton` (`"ParameterEditSetButton"`), `parameterEditCancelButton` (`"ParameterEditCancelButton"`) and `itemRevisionList` (`"ItemRevisionList"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each declaration with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S7.2. Ids: `static member kitItemRow (itemId : ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` is `KitItemRow_<the GUID>`; `addItemOffer (choice : ItemModelChoice)` is `AddItemOffer_<the entry GUID>_v<n>` for an item model or a sample and `AddItemOffer_<the preset's entry id>` for a preset; `newItemDialChoice (dial : ItemDial)` is `NewItemDial_Fixed`, `NewItemDial_Positive` or `NewItemDial_Negative`; `itemParameterRow (name : ParameterName)` is `ItemParameterRow_<the name>`; `itemRevisionRow (revision : ItemRevision)` is `ItemRevisionRow_<n>`. Captions, each `member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `ItemModelChoice` (an item model `<name> v<n>`, a preset its entry name, a sample `<name> v<n>`); `ItemDial` (`Fixed mounting`, `On a dial, sign +1`, `On a dial, sign −1`); `ItemRevisionRecord` (`Revision <n>: <name> <value>, …`, a known value, an unknown's start or a calibration's value). `ParameterGridCells = { state : ControlCaption; value : ControlCaption; bounds : ControlCaption; sigma : ControlCaption; provenance : ControlCaption }` and `type Parameter with member this.gridCells : ParameterGridCells`: a known value is `Known`, its value, `—`, `—`, `Given`; an unknown `Unknown`, its start, `[<lower>, <upper>]`, its prior's sigma or `—`, `To be fitted`; a calibration `Calibrated`, its value, `—`, its sigma, `Fit run <the fit run's name>`. Every number is `ToString("G6", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`, in the parameter's own unit (step 207). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `pickDataFile` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3376`) becomes public and takes `(title : ControlCaption)` after the owner, setting the picker options' `Title` to it; `attachDataFileButton` passes `ControlCaption "Attach measured-data file"`, today's title, so its picker is unchanged, and its doc says the Items panel's photo uses it too. On the model extension that holds `kitWrites` (step 185): `member model.itemModelCaption (item : Item) : ControlCaption` is the name the window's stores give the item's model: a preset's entry name through `model.library.tryGetEntry`, a sample's `<name> v<n>` through `model.samples.resolveVersion`, an item model's `<name> v<n>` through `model.itemModels.resolveItemModelVersion`, and `(model not in the library)` when the store answers `None` or an error. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ItemsPanelView`, compiled directly after `KitStartView.fs` (step 176) and before `KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and `itemsPanelView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`'s doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. The view is a `ScrollViewer`, both scroll bars `Auto`, over one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `itemsPanel`, margin 8, holding in order: (a) the semi-bold `Items` and the wrapping line `The physical pieces of this kit: each instantiates a library model and holds its own parameters.`; (b) while the kit's writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185) and no form is open, the verb `Add item from library model…` (`addItemButton`, sending `OpenAddItemForm`); (c) with a form open: `Choose a model:` over a `ScrollViewer` carrying `addItemOfferList`, vertical scroll bar `Auto`, `MaxHeight` 220, over the offers grouped under the semi-bold headings `Item models`, `Light sources`, `Polarizers` and `Samples` (a group with no offer shows nothing), each offer a box carrying `addItemOffer` with its caption sending `ChooseNewItemModel`; a `DockPanel` of `Label:` and a `TextBox` carrying `newItemLabelField` showing `labelText` whose every change sends `SetNewItemLabel`; `Dial:` and a `WrapPanel` of the three `newItemDialChoice` boxes (`FixedMounting`, `DialMounted DialPositive`, `DialMounted DialNegative`) with their captions sending `SetNewItemDial`; and one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Add` (`addItemConfirmButton`, `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, present only when the form's `itemDraftOpt` is `Some draft`, sending `AddItem draft`) and `Cancel` (`addItemCancelButton`, on `negativeBackground`, sending `CancelAddItemForm`), the action box's right margin being the gap; (d) a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitItemList`, one box per item of `kitItems` carrying `kitItemRow` and reading `<label> — <model.itemModelCaption item> — revision <n>`, sending `SelectKitItem`, or the line `This kit holds no item yet.`; (e) for the selected item: a `DockPanel` of `Label:` and a `TextBox` carrying `itemLabelField`, enabled by `kitWrites`, which on Enter or losing focus sends `RelabelKitItem` of `ItemLabel.tryCreate` of its text when that answers `Ok` with another label (a blank text is ignored, as `ExperimentControls`' number fields ignore an unreadable one); `Model: <itemModelCaption>` (`itemModelText`); `Dial: <dial.caption>` (`itemDialText`), the dial's zero being the `dialZero` row of the grid; `Notes:` and a wrapping `TextBox` carrying `itemNotesField`, accepting returns, enabled by `kitWrites`, which on losing focus sends `SetKitItemNotes` when its text changed; `Photo: <the kit path>` or `No photo` (`itemPhotoText`) with, while writes are offered, the verb `Choose photo…` (`itemChoosePhotoButton`), whose press resolves the owner window as `attachDataFileButton` does and calls `pickDataFile owner (ControlCaption "Choose item photo")` sending `SetKitItemPhoto`, and, when a photo is set, `Remove photo` (`itemRemovePhotoButton`, `RemoveKitItemPhoto`); a `Grid` carrying `itemParameterGrid`, six `Auto` columns `Parameter`, `State`, `Value`, `Bounds`, `σ` and `Provenance`, a semi-bold header row and one row per parameter in the item's order, whose first cell is a box carrying `itemParameterRow` with the name sending `EditItemParameter` and whose other cells are the parameter's `gridCells`; with `parameterEditOpt` open for this item, a block carrying `parameterEditPanel`: `Edit <name>`, a `WrapPanel` of `Known` (`parameterEditKnownChoice`) and `Unknown` (`parameterEditUnknownChoice`) sending `SetParameterEditChoice`, the labelled `TextBox`es `Value:` (or `Start:`), and for an unknown `Lower:`, `Upper:` and `Prior σ (blank: none):`, carrying their `parameterEdit…Field` ids, each change sending `SetParameterEditText`, the `describe` of `tryState`'s error in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, and one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Set` (`parameterEditSetButton`, `positiveBackground`, present only when `tryState` answers `Ok state` and writes are offered, sending `SetParameterState (item.id, name, state)`) and `Cancel` (`parameterEditCancelButton`, `negativeBackground`, `CancelParameterEdit`); and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `itemRevisionList`: `Revision <n> (current)` and then each `history` record, newest first, by its caption, each line carrying `itemRevisionRow` of its revision. A chosen offer, the chosen dial and state, and the selected item's row are `actionButton`s on `positiveBackground` and the others `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`s, the import dialog's chosen-option look (step 108). Every id is an AutomationId. A `WrapPanel` sits only in a vertical block (AGENTS.md). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ItemsPanelTests.fs`, `module ItemsPanelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `itemsPanelView` in a `HostWindow` as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` (`:107`) mounts a view, headless at 1000 × 700, over `initMain ()` driven through its messages (steps 239, 240). Without a trait: `the Items panel UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the fixed ids' texts, `kitItemRow` of a test-local GUID, `addItemOffer` of the circular polarizer's `LibraryModelChoice` (`AddItemOffer_33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b_v1`), `newItemDialChoice (DialMounted DialNegative)`, `itemParameterRow (ParameterName "c2.retardance")` (`ItemParameterRow_c2.retardance`) and `itemRevisionRow ItemRevision.first`. `the Items panel lists the kit's items and shows the selected item's model, dial, notes, photo, parameters and revisions`: with CPL1 (circular polarizer, `DialMounted DialPositive`) and LP1 added, CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` published as `CalibratedParameter` of 0.01 with sigma 0.002 from `FitRunName "QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z"` (step 235, set into `kitItems` by record update) and CPL1 selected: `kitItemList` holds CPL1's row then LP1's, CPL1's reading `CPL1 — Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder) v1 — revision 2`; `itemModelText` and `itemDialText` read `Model: Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder) v1` and `Dial: On a dial, sign +1`; the grid holds the five parameter rows, `c2.fastAxisOffset`'s reading `Calibrated`, `0.01`, `—`, `0.002` and `Fit run QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`; `itemRevisionList` holds revisions 2 and 1. `the add form lists the library models by kind and offers Add and Cancel on one row, Cancel to the right`: after `OpenAddItemForm`, `addItemOfferList` holds the circular polarizer's offer and `addItemConfirmButton` is absent; after a model and the label `CPL1`, `Add` and `Cancel` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Add's right. `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row`: after `EditItemParameter` of CPL1's `c2.retardance` and `SetParameterEditChoice UnknownStateChoice`, the lower, upper and prior fields are present; with the lower text `abc` the Set box is absent and the error is shown; with valid texts Set and Cancel have equal tops, Cancel to the right. `a kit opened read-only offers no item write in the Items panel`: over a model whose kit is the read-only view of a scratch kit holding CPL1 with a photo, `kitItems` CPL1 and CPL1 selected (record updates, as `ItemsPanelModelTests`' read-only facts build them, steps 239, 240), `addItemButton`, `itemChoosePhotoButton` and `itemRemovePhotoButton` are absent and `itemLabelField` and `itemNotesField` are disabled. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` (`:69`) does: `pressing Add item, a model, a label and Add records the item in the kit`: pressing `addItemButton`, the circular polarizer's offer, setting `newItemLabelField`'s text to `CPL1` and pressing `addItemConfirmButton` shows CPL1's `kitItemRow`, and the model's scratch kit's `readItems ()` answers CPL1. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The addItemOffer id and caption MUST always include the item-model GUID/version; a bound preset or sample MUST add its binding identity so two offers sharing one model remain distinct. Missing model resolution MUST render the typed missing-model condition, not a preset-only caption.

**Acceptance.** After the panel's view lands, `itemsPanelView` MUST show the kit's items, the add form, the selected item's label, model, dial, notes, photo, parameter grid, editor and revisions under their `ConstructorUiId`s, every write control withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add item, a model, a label and Add records the item in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Items panel UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Items panel lists the kit's items and shows the selected item's model, dial, notes, photo, parameters and revisions`, `the add form lists the library models by kind and offers Add and Cancel on one row, Cancel to the right`, `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row` and `a kit opened read-only offers no item write in the Items panel`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
